Proof-interface conclusion
  Hurwitz/Markov tells us how best-approximation exceptions are stratified.
  LRC14 asks for anti-approximation endpoint survival, so the direct scalar
  theorem is facing the wrong way.  The transferable object is the sidecar:
  continued-fraction period, Markov depth, quadratic unit, Pell carry, endpoint
  shell address, and named destroyed coordinates.  In HYP-3072 language this
  belongs to the blindness-pair/resonance-portfolio ledger.
